# The binary cycle density operator

The density operator of CPSV16 Example 4.11 (arXiv:1606.00608, lines 907–924), given by four
diagonal neighbouring operators on two-qubit sites. Its support carries a classical binary
cycle with coefficient matrix `W = !![1, 1/2; 1/2, 1]` and partition function
`tr(W^N) = (3^N + 1)/2^N`; the effective binary-support tensor is embedded into the ambient
two-qubit site by `k ↦ |k,k⟩`. Exact spectra on the ring of four sites give its block
entropies, which violate saturation of the area law, and exact two-site marginals on rings of
three and four sites refute zero correlation length. These are project derivations from the
printed operators, recorded in `docs/paper-gaps/cpsv16_examples_4_10_4_11_entropy.tex`.

## General theorems instantiated

* `MPOTensor.mpo_cyclicEdgeWeightTensor` (cyclic nearest-neighbour weights): the binary cycle is
  generated by one tensor of bond dimension four; arXiv:1606.00608, Appendix C.2,
  eq. `sigmaNK2`.
* `MPOTensor.blockEntropy_of_charpoly_roots_eq` (block entropies from spectra): the four
  block entropies on the ring of four sites.
* `MPOTensor.mutualInfoChain_eq_of_isSAL` (saturation of the area law): the unequal mutual
  informations show that the effective tensor is not `MPOTensor.IsSAL`; arXiv:1606.00608,
  Definition 4.6.
* `MPOTensor.isSAL_of_changePhysicalBasis_isSAL_of_isometry` (isometric physical inclusions):
  the failure of saturation transfers to the ambient two-qubit tensor; arXiv:1606.00608,
  Appendix C.2, lines 1733–1770.
* `MPOTensor.reducedBlockState_succ_succ_eq_succ_of_isSourceZCL` (marginal stability under zero
  correlation length): the marginals `14/41` and `5/14` show that the tensor is not
  `MPOTensor.IsSourceZCL`, as printed in the source; arXiv:1606.00608, Appendix C.2, line 1613.
-/
